Promote completed subagents into independent threads

Add saffron.promote_subagent to the owning root's tool set. It makes
a persistent idle root with the child's full native history and
effective settings, then closes the completed original subtree.

Require the source and its open descendants to be loaded, completed,
and free of pending work or terminal processes. Keep retirement tied
to each captured turn so later work retains its original owner.

Reserve the destination in Saffron storage before native creation,
and reuse it on retries. Report uncertain creation or incomplete
retirement with both thread IDs. Retirement can close some completed
descendants before a later member refuses shutdown. Native fork APIs own
copying; small session and agent-runtime seams own completion and teardown.
